From tru64-unix-managers  Tue May 30 06:59:38 1995
From: "Paul M. Collison" <p.collison1 () physics ! oxford ! ac ! uk>
Date: Tue, 30 May 1995 06:59:38 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Re: The OSF/1 3.2 FAQ revisited...
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075319906743


 Hi,

> I just upgraded to OSF/1 3.2 and ran into the problem anybody here seems to
> have:
> 
> Too many users logged on already.
> Try again later.
> rlogin: connection closed.
> 
> What is my problem? Do I have a wrong OSF-USR license?

 I had this problem. The implicit OSF-USR in OSF-BASE combines badly
 with a pre-existing OSF-USR.

 If prior to the upgrade your OSF-USR gave you many users, try this

 # lmf delete OSF-USR DEC OSF-BASE-IMPLICIT-USER
 # lmf reset

 You should then see something like

OSF-USR                   active                            unlimited

 and have no problems with numbers of logins.

 Cheers,

  Paul


