On Tue, 23 May 95 13:22:00 -0400  jrw@vlsi.bu.edu wrote:

> Now when ever I try either Mail or elm, it returns an error
> cannot lockf /usr/spool/mail/jrw.
> I tried to turn off NSF locking, (which sounds like a bad idea
> to me) but the mail programs won't work without locks.....

You are right. It is a *bad* idea to turn off NFS locking.

> 
> Is there anyway to fix this? Will this go away when I swap
> the server to an OSF machine in a few months?

Is NFS locking configured on both the mail client and the mail
server?

If not, make it so.

If so, try the following:

log in as root, and issue the following command:

# rcmgr set MAILLOCKING 5

Then reboot your system. This sets an entry in /etc/rc.config that will
allow both lockfile and lockf locking of a mail spool file.

Out of ideas if that doesn't work...

