you need in place of execute!)

	the command sequence in the server config runs something along the lines
of:

		change port all telnet client .....

			(I'm lacking docs here, but the built in help WAS very helpful!)


		Jim

>From hagan@oec.comMon May 15 08:26:29 1995

If i remember correctly, the termcap under OSF/1 is a little
wonky. if you have access to an ultrix box -- or any other
BSD style system, try replacing your /etc/termcap

-- craig

>From bgk1142@bggfu2.nho.hydro.comTue May 16 08:05:32 1995

The moment I heard of 'won't recognise CTRL-X' the bell rang.

I had similar problems earlier, all related to emacs and users logging in
from a DECserver via TCP/IP (Telnet). The solution was to configure the
DECserver to recognise CTRL-X (maybe your other problems can be solved by
reviewing the DECserver configuration too) and not just drop it.
