Subject: Re: Where are my X-windows?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075319906548

You need to add this line in your config (ie /usr/sys/conf/"HOSTNAME"):
controller      fb0        at tc0       slot  0 vector    fbint

this line tells the system that there is a controller in slot0 and that it is
a frame buffer card.  If the card is not in slot0 that entry needs to reflect 
which slot your frame buffer card is in.

I hope this helps?

