On Wed, 10 May 1995, J.Amon wrote:

> Sorry to post this to an unrelated list, but you guys are wonderfully
> helpful.
> 
> Can I run two httpd servers on different ports, with different
> base directories, from the same Alpha/OSF machine? I'm using
> NCSA httpd and OSF 3.0.

No problem at all - you'll need to maintain two seperate httpd.conf 
files, one for each port.  There is pretty much nothing to it - you'll 
simply run two seperate httpd processes.

You can also run two on the same port by multihoming your network 
interface.  Look for "Two Servers, one Interface" on yahoo (under 
computers->internet->worldwideweb->servers or something like that).  I'd 
tell you the URL but yahoo isn't responding right now :-(.

Good luck...

- Al

