X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075319906498

The original query was:

	How can I determine the FlashROM firmware revision level 
	from the console monitor prompt?

	
The SHOW CONFIG command shows this, although rather obscurely, and it
is not documented in the Hardware Reference Guide.  The SHOW CONFIG
command produces output something like this:

	DEC 3000 - M300
	Digital Equipment Corporation
		VPP PAL blah blah blah ...
		Built on 30-MAR-1993 blah blah blah

	TCINFO	  DEVNAM	DEVSTAT
	------    ------        -------------------------------------
		     CPU	OK KN16-AA - Vx.x-Syyy-Izzz - sx.x - ....


The first occurence of the string x.x above is replaced with the firmware 
revision level.  I discovered this after looking at several machines which 
I knew to have different revision levels.

It would be nice if Digital would include a legend for the symbols x.x,
yyy, and zzz in the Hardware Reference Manual.  

--
Carl Harris
Systems Engineer
Department of Computer Science, Virginia Tech
ceharris@cs.vt.edu

