To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY & SOLUTION - UNIX 3.2 NFS server hanged by AIX clients
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075319906495

Hi,

It appears there was a real problem when AIX clients are mounting
filesystem from DIGITAL UNIX 3.2. After they did a  'find' on the
mounted filesystem, it hanged the network traffic of the nfs server.
As far as I found out, it happens only when the server uses FDDI.

The SOLUTION supplied by DEC engineering :

 use mount ... -o noacl ... on the aix client.

It appears the same problem happens also on some SUN servers connected
to AIX clients.

regards
kobi.

