From tru64-unix-managers  Wed May 10 05:39:11 1995
From: Alex A Sergejew <alex () ecco ! bsee ! swin ! edu ! au>
Date: Wed, 10 May 1995 05:39:11 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Perl5.001 dumps core under OSF/1 v3.2
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96075319906484

On Tue, 9 May 1995 20:10:13 +1000
I asked the alpha-osf-managers list:

>... the problem is that perl compiles OK and passes
>the test scripts, even runs most of the old perl scripts I've tried it on,
>but on trying to make the perlref stuff I get core dumps

I am indebted to the following wizards:
	Guy Helmer <ghelmer@alpha.dsu.edu>
	John Stoffel <john@WPI.EDU>
	Mike Iglesias <iglesias@draco.acs.uci.edu>
	Spider Boardman <spider@orb.nashua.nh.us>
who all kindly responded with much the same advice which solved the problem.

It turns out that there are a series of "unofficial" patches to perl5.001
(so far comprising patches 1a through 1e) which are not found in most of
the standard perl5.0001.tar.gz distribution sets.  These patches are
being maintained by Andy Dougherty <doughera@lafcol.lafayette.edu>
and are available (among other places) from:
