> need 1.74 tapes.  It seems to think the tape is a TK50 or something.
> As far as I know the tape I inserted was a standard DLT CompacTape III.
> What did I do wrong?  Also, what do people usually use for a blocking
> factor (b) for DLT2000's?  It also seemed it was taking a while 
> compared to what I expected...

Here, we always just specify 'B 2100000' on our dump command line,
since 2 Gig is Ultrix's maximum file system size.  We've had no
problems doing this for the last few years...

A few simple tests here on a DLT showed that a 32k blocking factor
produces good results.  Going over 32k made very little difference.

> Thanks for any help.
> Chela Kunasz

Simon.

