>From iglesias@draco.acs.uci.edu Wed May  3 12:05:54 1995

You first need to look at the system to see what is using the space.
If you're using a lot X clients or something that allocates large bitmaps,
your X server may be growing.  If that is the case, put the following line

DisplayManager*terminateServer: true

in /usr/lib/X11/xdm/xdm-config and either reboot the system or type:

  kill -HUP `cat /usr/lib/X11/xdm/xdm-pid`

This will cause the X server to be restarted after each user logs out.

If the X server is not the problem, you'll have to figure out what is.
Using 'ps augxww' is a good place to start.


Mike

