>From alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com Wed May  3 14:17:11 1995

	It sounds like you're *using* swap space instead of losing
	it.  Having swap space used is normal, since all virtual
	memory allocations require the reservation or at least
	usage of page/swap space.  If the space is still gone after
	the users have logged out and all the processes they have
	started are gone, then you might need to worry.

	If particular applications seem to continue growing without
	apparent need, then you may want to check the application for
	memory leaks.
